Subject: [PATCH RFC 0/2] media: i2c: dw9719: manage optional I/O supply
To: Sakari Ailus <sakari.ailus@linux.intel.com>
Cc: Griffin Kroah-Hartman <griffin.kroah@fairphone.com>,
    André Apitzsch <git@apitzsch.eu>,
    Luca Weiss <luca.weiss@fairphone.com>,
    linux-media@vger.kernel.org,
    devicetree@vger.kernel.org

On Surface Pro 11, the DW9800K's 2.9 V VDD and its 1.8 V
I/O supply are independent. The latter shares PM8010 L6M with the
OV13858 rear camera sensor's DOVDD. The VCM will not answer CCI
transactions when that I/O rail is down, and forcing L6M always-on
is undesirable.

This RFC models the I/O supply as an optional vddio regulator consumer
of the dw9719 driver. The actuator enables vddio before VDD, releases
it after VDD, and properly unwinds both supplies on failures. Boards
without the property retain their existing behavior.

Hardware validation on an X1E80100 Surface Pro 11 OLED with the
experimental downstream CCI/CAMSS and rear-camera DT:
- DW9800K bound independently of OV13858 and accepted focus controls.
- PM8010 L6M enable count: 0 with both devices idle; 1 with the
  sensor streaming alone; 2 when sensor and VCM were both open;
  then 1 on VCM close while streaming; finally 0 on stream stop.
- L16B VCM VDD became idle after the VCM was closed, without
  interrupting ongoing OV13858 streaming.
- OV13858 RAW10 capture: 4224x3136 around 30 fps, sensor V4L2
  compliance 46/46. The VCM compliance test was 45/46 (existing
  control-event subscription limitation).
- Four successful Linux pm_test=devices callback cycles followed by
  focus writes and 30-frame captures. This is not a claim of full
  system suspend or optical focus-quality validation.

This test used the original pre-v4 DW9719 driver plus the optional
vddio patch. We ALSO built and live-tested the driver change alongside
the separately posted DW9800K v4 cleanup (2026-11-19): successful
probe/focus control and idle L6M/L16B off. Because that series
proposes a separate dongwoon,dw9800k.yaml binding, its binding needs
a corresponding vddio-supply property. The v4 series is under
review and the DT ABI discussion remains open, so this RFC targets
the pinned pre-v4 mainline base; please advise preferred integration
order once that series settles.

The exact PM8010 L6M input parent on Denali is not schematic-proven;
board-level DTS is deliberately excluded from this driver RFC.

